{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrictComplementarityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrictComplementarityPair","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L88-L97","doc":"**Trivial strict-complementarity pair** for the constraint-\nfree case.  The active set is empty (no constraints to be\nactive), so `active_dual_pos` and `inactive_dual_zero` both\nhold vacuously. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.instHasStrongDualityEmpty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.instHasStrongDualityEmpty","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L82-L86","doc":"**Strong duality holds for the constraint-free case** —\ninstance form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.trivialStrongDualityPair","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L60-L80","doc":"**Strong-duality witness for the constraint-free case**: take\nthe primal optimum to be `0 : Matrix _ _ R` (vacuously feasible\nwhen constraints are empty), the dual optimum to be the empty\nfunction, and observe that primal and dual objectives both\nequal `0`.\n\nPER COPILOT REVIEW: this construction is only valid as an\n\"optimum\" when the primal infimum is attained at 0, which\nrequires `sdp.cost` to have a non-negative direction (i.e.\nPSD).  For costs with negative directions the infimum is\n`-∞`.  The `StrongDualityPair`'s `obj_eq` field is `True`\nso this construction is technically well-typed even without\nPosSemidef cost; downstream consumers should confirm cost\nsemidefiniteness before relying on the \"optimum\" claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.one_isStrictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.one_isStrictlyFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The identity matrix is strictly feasible for any constraint-free\nSDP (positive-definite, no constraints to satisfy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.zero_isFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDPEmptyConstraints.zero_isFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDPEmptyConstraints.lean#L47-L51","doc":"For any `SDPPrimal n R Empty`, the zero matrix is feasible\n(vacuously satisfies all constraints). ","signatureChunk":0}]}